Limit the sharpen-at-rest repaint to what the user can actually see
(WEBKIT_LOWRES_SHARPEN_VIEWPORT_ONLY, default OFF).

When scroll degradation ends, every tile still at low resolution is invalidated
WHOLE and repainted at full resolution -- including the prepaint cushion. With
the default cover multiplier of 2, roughly half the tiles held are outside the
viewport and were never looked at. The repaint lands exactly when the user has
stopped scrolling, so it is felt as a stutter at rest.

This is the fixed cost that makes marginal engagement a losing trade, and three
independent measurements point at it:

  * halving how often the tier armed changed the cheap page's penalty by NOTHING
    (85.5% -> 43.0% armed; p95, jank and raster CPU identical to three digits);
  * a barely-degraded 0.90 scale still paid the entire +1.9pp jank penalty;
  * partial engagement (43-46% armed) was worse on some metrics than either
    extreme, because each engage/disengage cycle pays a whole repaint.

The cost is per ENGAGEMENT, not per unit of degradation, because every engagement
ends in one of these repaints.

With the flag on, only tiles intersecting the viewport inflated by
WEBKIT_LOWRES_SHARPEN_MARGIN_PX (default 512, ~one tile row) are sharpened at
rest. Cushion tiles keep isLowRes and are picked up by the same pass once the
viewport plus margin reaches them -- it runs on every non-degrading update, so a
tile is sharpened before it becomes visible and nothing is left soft on screen.
Deliberately does not set m_pendingTileCreation for deferred tiles: there is no
work to finish until the viewport moves, and re-arming the poll would spin.

Note this helps the LEGACY SPEED LADDER exactly as much as the cost trigger --
the sharpen pass is shared by both, so the A/B is worth running either way.

Not attempted: skipping the sharpen for tiles painted at a near-1.0 scale. Under
the shipped calibration WEBKIT_LOWRES_COST_ENGAGE_X=2.0 caps the derived scale at
1/sqrt(2) ~ 0.707, so that case cannot arise and the check would be dead code.

Must apply after webkit-lowres-cost-trigger.patch (same file).

UPDATE (build 627): **default flipped ON**, device-validated by the user.
Measured on 626 with the cost trigger active, 4 reps interleaved:

  instrument   531 tiles sharpened vs 2172 deferred -- 80% of the repaint avoided
  heavy        fps 37.1->39.3 (+5.9%), p95 50.0->48.5, rasterCPU 75.8->70.2
  multilayer   fps 29.2->30.9 (+6.0%), p95 60.5->54.0 (-10.7%), jank 21.8->18.1

Per-arm fps spreads non-overlapping on both. Caveat recorded in INVESTIGATION.md
C14: vel_p50 differed between arms (scrollY read-back lags when the compositor is
behind), and the viewport arm scrolled LESS, so the magnitude is probably
optimistic. The mechanism is not confounded -- the tile count is measured
engine-side, independent of input emulation, and raster CPU moves as it predicts.

